			<div class="content" id="post-content-4861352">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
The Foundation doesn't normally treat SCP's compassionately or particularly humanely. But when a dangerous anomaly shows a sliver of humanity and has valuable people hostage, the Foundation has to rush to turn a monster into a caring person.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
A dangerous anomaly launches an unexpected attack on a Foundation facility, injuring a number of key individuals including the Site Director. It is incapacitated when it falters in attacking a pregnant woman. The Foundation discovers that the anomaly may kill the injured individuals at any point via its anomalous effect. The anomaly decides that violence is not the best way to go about its goal and demands access to sensitive documents under threat of the death of its victims. The Foundation, citing its failure attack the pregnant woman, theorizes that the anomaly may have a slight compassion for humanity, and sets a psychiatrist/therapist on the case to attempt and bring that to the forefront.</p>
<p><strong>Hook:</strong><br />
The main idea I want to run with is a normally callous Foundation having to do its absolute best to make an anomaly care about the people around it.</p>

